---
/* The pointer used inside product clips.

   Redrawn to the real thing. The previous one was a thin hollow triangle that
   read as an arrowhead rather than a cursor; this is the standard desktop
   pointer — the notched tail on the right edge is the detail that makes it
   recognisable, and it is the part the old one was missing.

   Appearance only. Every clip owns its own path and its own click ring, drawn
   on the positioned wrapper it sits in — a shared cursor that also carried its
   choreography would have to know about every graphic it appears in.

   Drawn rather than imaged so it stays crisp at whatever size the graphic
   renders at, and so it can carry the drop shadow that separates it from a
   white card underneath. */
---

<svg class="cur" viewBox="0 0 20 28" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
  <path
    d="M2.4 1.6 17.2 15.1h-6.5l-1 .3 3.1 7.4-3 1.3-3.1-7.4-4.3 4.2Z"
    fill="var(--white)"
    stroke="var(--neutral-100)"
    stroke-width="1.5"
    stroke-linejoin="round"
  />
</svg>

<style>
  .cur {
    display: block;
    inline-size: 4.4cqw;
    block-size: auto;
    filter: drop-shadow(0 1px 3px rgb(from var(--neutral-100) r g b / 0.32));
  }
</style>
